<</AP<</N 777 0 R >>/Border[ 0 0 0]/Contents(Theoretically, we can solve, in the same way that has be done in 90s, using Automatic Updates. Practically, we can't because of two main aspects: \(1\)Technical and \(2\)Liability.\n1\) Even if the devices are the same, the conditions in which the device is installed and used are different \(same for configuration\) \(example: fixing a vulnerability and pushing an update with the fix for a device. While the update may work for most, it can "brick" or disable others, rendering them operationally dead and creating a self-inflicted denial-of-service.\)\n2\) If an automatic update starts and triggers a failure during peak business hours, the resulting downtime can be devastating. \(example: security camera or automatic doors open with digital keys: it compromises physical security and halts business operations.\))/DA( /Helv 8.625 Tf -0.375 Tc 9.66 TL 0 0.466667 0.831373 rg )/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Rect[ 138.048706 5.7983398 581.65973 81.790771]/Rotate 0/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
endobj
